      "message": "This explanation isn\u0027t quite right: `bl log_printf` and `bl cflush` are calls made from `test_crash()` that overwrite `LR` (`test_crash()`\u0027s incoming `LR` was pushed to the stack in its prologue), so `LR` does not hold the return address into `test_crash()`\u0027s caller.\n\nInstead, `cflush()` (via `uart_flush_output()` -\u003e `uart_tx_flush()`) is a non-leaf function: it pushes `lr` to the stack, makes internal `bl`/`blx` calls (such as `uart_irq_tx_complete()`, setting `LR` to an address inside `uart_tx_flush()`), and returns via `pop {..., pc}`. Because popping into `PC` does not restore `LR`, `LR` still points inside `uart_tx_flush()`/`cflush()` when the inlined `__builtin_trap()` executes in `test_crash()`.",
